en  experience a 96 percent decrease to air  travel you end up  with four percent of the air travel you  started with you start with something  you take away 96 percent you're left  with four percent if you then increase  air travel by a hundred and twenty  percent air travel is still down 91  percent from where it was this is just a  common function of how percentages and  growth rates work if you lose 50 percent  of something you need to gain 100  percent to get back to where you were if  I have $100 in stock and that stock  loses 50% of its value my hundred  dollars is now worth $50 to get back to  $100  I need that 50 bucks to increase 100  percent and this is the crux of a ton of  the disinformation propaganda propaganda  garbage math that you are going to be  hit with over the next few months as the  recovery hopefully starts to happen  depending on how deadly coronavirus  remains and how bad wave 2 is you are  going to see a lot of this stuff I'll  give you some other examples jobs have  so imploded that they will start using  job growth numbers that will be  meaningless because of the base numbers  that are being used understand that we  lost more than 20% of our workforce so  far we might recover 5% of the current  workforce and they will say hey we're  already a quarter of the way back that's  not how growth rates work if you lose  20% of the workforce and then you gain  back 5% of that reduced number you're  only gaining 19% of what you lost not  twenty five so understand how these  growth rates work the one that will  really be weaponized is probably going  to be GDP we in all likelihood are going  to see historic GDP lost numbers for the  second quarter in the United States  we're not going to get those numbers  until sometime in August most likely so  normally the numbers would be for  example like OGD P and Q two went up  point five percent usually you annualize  that so 0.5 percent over four  would be like on track for 2% GDP growth  for the year oka